  { label: 'h3', id: 'section-13', content: "Variants" },
  { label: 'p', content: "<code>inset</code> (default) embeds the indicator in an opaque track with a permanent 1px stroke ring and shadow; <code>raised</code> has a track with no ring or shadow, and the indicator floats above it with a soft shadow. Both variants share the same interaction and text color." },
  { label: 'p', content: "Invalid values fall back to <code>inset</code>." },
  { label: 'p', content: "Integration with the native <code>&lt;form></code>: <code>name</code> submits the current value and <code>form.reset()</code> restores the initial value." },
  { label: 'p', content: "The component syncs the child triggers' <code>checked</code> state from <code>value</code>. <code>disabled</code> gives the whole group an inherited effective disabled state without rewriting the triggers' own <code>disabled</code> attribute. Setting <code>value</code> directly dispatches no events." },
  { label: 'p', content: "Keyboard users press Tab into the currently selected item; with no selection, the first enabled item receives focus. Only that one item in the group participates in the tab order." },
  { label: 'p', content: "In a horizontal group, ArrowLeft / ArrowRight move focus cyclically among enabled items and update the selection; Home / End move to the first / last enabled item; disabled items are skipped." },
  { label: 'p', content: "ArrowUp / ArrowDown do not move focus." },
  { label: 'p', content: "Holding the current item and dragging horizontally slides the indicator, and releasing snaps to the nearest option; a fast flick switches by velocity." },
  { label: 'p', content: "When trigger widths differ, the dragging indicator takes the width of the item closest to its own center, which is the item the release would land on. It does not keep the width of the pressed item." },
  { label: 'p', content: "The touch surface declares <code>touch-action: none</code> and blocks the default <code>touchmove</code> scroll while a drag is active, so iOS Safari does not interrupt the gesture." },
  { label: 'h3', id: 'section-14', content: "Pressed state" },
  { label: 'p', content: "Both variants share the same pressed / drag state: the indicator turns into a transparent glass surface (blur, stroke ring, and 1.5x scale) that settles on the first frame of the press and fades back to its own idle surface on release." },
  { label: 'h3', id: 'section-15', content: "Label color" },
  { label: 'p', content: "All labels use <code>--wui-color-text</code>; selected and unselected items keep the same color, the selection is still carried by the indicator, and no label uses <code>--wui-color-accent</code>. Under the built-in light/dark themes, 14px text meets 4.5:1." }
